WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.620
Japan is to economics what Axl Rose is to
music business.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:17.300
They both rocked in the late 80s and beginning of the 90s, then they started losing ground

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.470
and nowadays, anytime they try to make a comeback, the results are… pretty disappointing.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:33.080
I know what you are thinking… from the first
glance, Japan doesn’t seem to be that bad,

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.080
right?

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.340
They have the videogames, the anime movies
and world class tech behemoths.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:42.010
And their capital, Tokyo, looks like a Scy-Fy
city.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:46.010
It is the World’s biggest metropolis, with
over 30 M people, and they have the fastest

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:50.010
trains, the most modern TVs and even human-like
robots.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:56.020
Nonetheless, this country has been 2 decades
without no economic growth.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.399
And this is not the worst!

00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:00.570
Japan is the most indebted country in the
whole planet.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:02.719
They owe more than twice their entire GDP.

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:07.039
And their population is decreasing faster
than anywhere else, which poses a big problem

00:01:07.039 --> 00:01:09.600
in order to pay retirement pensions.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.790
This is one of the reasons why Japanese workers
make crazy hours and have almost no vacations.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:19.070
And those good old technological juggernauts
like HITACHI or PANASONIC are falling behind

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:25.190
the more modern companies from China or America.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:30.290
But hold on just a second because things might
change!

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:43.870
Yes, I’m talking about the TOKYO OLIMPICS,
2020.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:50.130
A peerless opportunity to make to showcase
the whole country and get the world’s attention.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:56.409
Yes, my dear viewers… since Japan won the
Olimpic bid, in the year 2013, tourism has

00:01:56.409 --> 00:01:57.600
skyrocketed from one day to the other.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.310
And the same goes with private investment.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:04.060
By that year 2020, Tokyo will have 45 brand
new skyscrapers.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.009
Nothing more and nothing less.

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:13.730
And companies like PANASONIC will set state
of the art solar cells all over the place

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.180
so people can charge their electric cars.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:21.920
If this was not enough, SONY will launch their
brand new 8K TV screens.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.200
Yep, you heard that right.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.310
If 4K was not enough, now we will have 8K
so you will be able to see even the microfiber

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.069
of the athletes Tshirts.

00:02:29.069 --> 00:02:33.400
But hold on just a second because… not everything
is as beautiful!

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:39.180
You see, when Tokyo won the Olympic bid, they
budgeted them in 6.5 billion dollars.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:43.680
But once they started with the building, the
costs have doubled.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:44.780
And they haven’t even finished!

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:50.239
In fact, Tokyo’s city hall has predicted
the total cost might end up near the 20 billion

00:02:50.239 --> 00:02:51.239
USD.

00:02:51.239 --> 00:02:55.830
So the question is… would this Summer Olympic
Games be an opportunity for Japan… or the

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:56.830
opposite?

00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:01.060
Are Olympic Games as good for a country’s
economy as some people say?

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:08.519
Today we are gonna answer all of this questions
but, before, let’s take a look back at history.

00:03:08.519 --> 00:03:11.680
AN OLYMPIC FALACY?

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.760
Few things spark nacional pride as much as
Olympic games.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.790
Of course, we all like to brag about the gold
medals our country has.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:29.500
But what really inflames patriotism the most
is to become an Olympic host.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:34.099
The excitement it generates is so big that
everyone, regardless of their ideology, seems

00:03:34.099 --> 00:03:38.879
to think that organizing an event like this
is a good thing for the country.

00:03:38.879 --> 00:03:41.299
Nonetheless, inside the economists field,
things are not that clear.

00:03:41.299 --> 00:03:45.840
In fact… the arguments in favour of hosting
Olympics are a little bit like… hmm… how

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:46.840
should I say?

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:50.650
They are so inconsistent they could be a tweet
written by Donald Trump

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:55.720
According to a paper from the Bank of Japan,
the effects of the Olympics are so good that

00:03:55.720 --> 00:04:01.330
you can tell even before they have been celebrated.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:08.430
More specifically, the same year the International
Olympic Committee named Tokyo as the host

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:12.790
city, everyone started to see Japan as a perfect
place for investment.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:17.549
Remember that we are talking about a paper
from an institution as prestigious as the

00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:18.910
Bank of Japan.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:22.830
This would be the Japanese equivalent to the
American Federal Reserve.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:27.500
This said, one of their main arguments is
that, if your city gets to be an Olympic host,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.800
the whole country can join all those big organizations
every country would like to be a member of.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:32.800
Want examples?

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:33.800
Here you have examples!

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.570
Barcelona got the nomination in 1986 and…

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:36.570
BOOM!

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:38.220
That very same year, they joined the European
Union.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:40.100
Beijing was nominated in 2001 and…

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.100
BOOM!

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.480
That year they joined the World Trade Organization.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:43.640
What do you say?

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:46.330
It seems like nobody could argue this train
of thoughs, right?

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:51.530
Well… wait a second because this is a textbook
example of a correlation fallacy.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:55.150
In other words, the fact that Spain joined
the EU the same year Barcelona got chosen

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:59.400
as the Olympic host does not mean one thing
caused the other.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:05.270
In fact, Portugal also joined the EU on the
same year without hosting anything.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:08.850
And the same happened with China.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:13.479
On the same times, other Asian countries joined
the WTO without organizing no sport events.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.740
But I know what you are gonna tell me now!

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:20.660
Hey Simon, what about the international attention?

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:25.440
During two weeks, the whole world is going
to put their eyes in Japan.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:29.770
We are talking about the biggest sport event
in the world.

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:31.000
Or maybe not?

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:43.660
You see, the London Olympics 2012 got an average
audience of, around 31 million people in America.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:47.990
To make a comparison, this is twice as much
as a Game of Thrones episode.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:49.870
Yes, it’s not bad.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.640
But… what happened with the rest of the
games?

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:55.669
For example, Sochi Winter Olympics, 2014,
didn’t even get to have 22 million viewers

00:05:55.669 --> 00:05:56.669
in the States.

00:05:56.669 --> 00:06:00.130
And Rio 2016 was around 26 million.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:05.389
This might look big to you, guys, but is nothing
if we compare it with a much cheaper event

00:06:05.389 --> 00:06:08.150
like the SUPERBOWL.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:14.910
The 2016 Superbowl surpassed 110 million viewers.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:18.889
In other words, even though Olympics are watched
all around the world, when you look at the

00:06:18.889 --> 00:06:22.560
audiences country by country, the figures
are not so impressive.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:26.330
And this means that the perception that people
have about a country does not change.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:29.960
At least, it doesn’t change… for good…

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:37.150
In a study of the impact of the 2000 Olympics
in Sydney, Australian researchers interviewed

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:40.300
people one year before and after the Games.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:46.270
They found little change in perceptions, with
one surprising wrinkle: South Africans had

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:51.710
soured on Australia “because of the way
in which the Aboriginal issue was highlighted

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:56.449
and portrayed by the South African media,”

00:06:56.449 --> 00:07:04.310
Nonetheless, there is one thing where it seems
fair to agree: Olympic games kickstart your

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:05.520
tourism industry.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.319
Actually, since Tokyo was chosen as the Olympic
host, tourism in Japan has skyrocketed.

00:07:09.319 --> 00:07:16.199
They almost didn’t have tourists in 2013
and now they surpassed 24 million people last

00:07:16.199 --> 00:07:17.199
year.

00:07:17.199 --> 00:07:20.110
You can say a brand new industry has been
born in Japan.

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:25.440
And this is an industry that attracts lots
of foreign money…

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:29.090
Who wouldn’t be happy with this?

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:33.720
Well… hold on a minute because even this
figures can be argued.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.169
Of course, tourism in Japan has increased
a lot.

00:07:36.169 --> 00:07:42.580
But… do you know of other countries with
a booming tourism sector? Chile and Thailand.

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:45.509
They have grown at a similar rate as Japan.

00:07:45.509 --> 00:07:49.580
And… don’t even google it because I will
tell you here: none of this two countries

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:54.330
is planning to host any Olympics.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:58.240
The Thailand example is pretty paradigmatic.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:03.910
They get 6 million more tourists than Japan
with half of its population.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:08.240
And their tourism growth is directly correlated
to that of the Chinese middle class.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:13.520
In other words, as Chinese people have more
money, they want to do sight seeing… and

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:14.759
where do they go?

00:08:14.759 --> 00:08:15.759
Of course!

00:08:15.759 --> 00:08:19.069
They go to countries that are nearby and have
beautiful things to see!

00:08:19.069 --> 00:08:21.259
But I know what you are thinking!

00:08:21.259 --> 00:08:25.860
Despite the Olympics not being that profitable
as they seem… what’s the problem if Tokyo

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.260
wants to have Olympics?

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:30.440
Who doesn’t like to have a giant stadium
on his city, huh?

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:35.620
Well… let’s have a look at this right
now.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:38.020
GOLD MEDALLIST…

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:39.120
IN SPENDING!

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:40.310
We all know it…

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:41.409
Olympics are costly.

00:08:41.409 --> 00:08:46.800
From one day to the other, Tokyo will have
to build an Olympic Stadium to host more than

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.470
80,000 people.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:53.360
And also, they have to impress them with lights
and colors.

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:55.220
But it doesn’t stop here!

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:59.500
They need other special venues for the many
competitions that are held at the same time.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:00.900
Each of the sports have its own specifications.

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.120
Athletism requires different things than swimming
or canoeing.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:11.020
In summary, 31 venues will be built or remodelated
for this Tokyo 2020 Summer Olympic Games.

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:18.029
Add to this the media centre, which is another
big White Elephant and, on the top of it,

00:09:18.029 --> 00:09:19.029
the Olympic Villa.

00:09:19.029 --> 00:09:23.421
This is short of a small town where more than
10,000 athelets will live during the time

00:09:23.421 --> 00:09:24.421
the Olympics are held.

00:09:24.421 --> 00:09:27.920
And, as you can imagine, this will not be
cheap, either.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.540
The total cost for this was meant to be 6.5
billion USD.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:35.670
At least, this is the figure given by the
local authorities to the International Olympic

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.540
Committee in 2013.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:46.740
But, you know, one thing is the theory and
another thing is the reality…

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:50.750
Tokyo 2020 Olympic Games costs just keep rising

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:56.890
By December 2017, Tokyo City Hall had already
spent over 12 billions.

00:09:56.890 --> 00:10:00.940
And just a couple of months later, the local
authorities said that, at least, they will

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:04.550
end up spending 20 billiones!

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:11.079
And maybe, this figure will keep rising before
they burn the Olympic flame…

00:10:11.079 --> 00:10:13.990
In fact, nothing of this is a surprise.

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:17.560
Since we have memory, every Olympic Games
have cost overrun.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:21.899
And we are not talking about little pennies
here!

00:10:21.899 --> 00:10:27.040
Rio de Janeiro 2016 ended up being 51% more
expensive than expected.

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:35.279
But the record, so far, is Montreal 1976,
that costed 700% more than the initial budget.

00:10:35.279 --> 00:10:36.279
Yes, you heard this right.

00:10:36.279 --> 00:10:39.010
This is 8 times more that what it was planned
at the beginning.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:40.300
And now you might wonder…

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:44.329
All this billion dollars are little or big
money for a government?

00:10:44.329 --> 00:10:49.180
I mean… compared with the normal spending
in a big city hall… is this a big number?

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:51.850
Well, the answer is a big YES.

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:56.210
For a better understanding, with 20 billion
USD you could build, for instance, a highway

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:59.670
that connected the extreme north of Japan
to their extreme South.

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:03.959
But wait a minute because this is not the
worst of all!

00:11:03.959 --> 00:11:10.370
You see… an airport or a highway can and
up being a waste of money.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.810
But, still, you can always reutilize it.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:16.130
A country with better infrastructures and
communication can have better companies in

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:18.990
the future, brand new industries or better
public services.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:22.589
But what do you do with an Olympic stadium
that can host 80,000 people?

00:11:22.589 --> 00:11:29.519
Well… if we look at past examples, the answer
is pretty much bitter…

00:11:29.519 --> 00:11:34.089
Rio Olympic venues already falling into a
state of disrepair

00:11:34.089 --> 00:11:37.089
Rio de Janeiro example is pretty harsh.

00:11:37.089 --> 00:11:41.990
Despite having Olympics, they still have entire
neighbourhoods that are not even connected

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:44.279
to the city centre by a bus line.

00:11:44.279 --> 00:11:46.840
And the place where the Olympic Villa has
is becoming a slum.

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:52.210
But wait a minute because this is not the
only example.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:58.850
Athens Olympic site in ruins 10 years on from
2004 Games

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:02.000
Add to this the fact that Japan is the most
indebted country in the planet.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:05.250
They owe a sum equivalent to 230% of their
GDP.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:09.100
The government is already struggling to pay
the retirement pensions and they have been

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:14.100
2 years without any economic growth whatsoever.

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:18.670
So now this is your turn…

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:23.160
Do you think the Tokyo Olympics 2020 will
mean the ruin of Japan?

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:27.269
Or maybe, against the odds, Japan will take
some advantage of hosting this event?

00:12:27.269 --> 00:12:29.450
Please, leave your answer in the comment section
below.

